  "published": "2026-09-25T10:43:14.33Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "LC009 is quieter on real code: it no longer reports queries whose entities the method returns to its caller (set dotnet_code_quality.LC009.report_returned_entities = true to report them again), nor a Join or GroupJoin that projects only scalars, and it sees writes through a ?? new fallback; on Kavita its reports fall from 157 to 34. Code-fix safety fixes from applying the fixes to real applications: LC009 withholds AsNoTracking() when entities reached through a navigation are passed on or stored; LC002 no longer moves filters on computed or [NotMapped] properties into SQL; fixes that add a using (LC001, LC004, LC006, LC007, LC008, LC009, LC012, LC015, LC017, LC032, LC033, LC041, LC042, LC045, LC047 and LC051) skip one a global using already provides and place it below a copyright header; LC001, LC006, LC015 and LC017 keep the inserted call on the source line in multi-line queries; LC043 keeps comments above the removed declaration; LC042 no longer duplicates a #pragma; LC026 no longer passes an outer token into a static lambda or local function; LC008 is not offered inside a lock or unsafe context.",
